Z||000000||Black86SE||11-28-2001||12:41 AM||||What 5-speed trannys were avaliable in '86 on the 4cyl manuals? I need to know cause I might be buying parts for my tranny swap and I want to make sure the parts will fit my isuzu. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Black86SEsig_1.gif"> <BR>Black 1986 SE V6<BR>Automatic - 5-speed soon!<BR>17" Motegi MR7 Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS<BR>AIM ScreenName: Black86se||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-28-2001||08:15 AM||||I believe all (stock) 5-speed Fieros with 4-cylinder engines had Isuzu transaxles.  Does that answer your question?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eriamjh||11-28-2001||05:29 PM||||Does the same apply to '87 coupes with 4 cylinders?<P>If not, how can you tell which one is in your car?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-28-2001||06:40 PM||||All '85-'88 4-cyl. Fieros came with the Isuzu 5-sp.  It is highly doubtful that anyone transplanted a Getrag into a coupe, so I think it's a safe bet that it will also have an Isuzu.  <P>One way to tell is by the shifter and selector cables......Isuzu cables have a foam covering and teh Getrag has a cloth (covered by foil) covering.<P>Also, the Getrag 5-speeds have dipsticks and the Isuzus do not.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black86SE||11-28-2001||10:26 PM||||Cool, answers my questions. Thanks you two.||||reg||1
